# Recorded Playwright reports are evidence, not source.
#
# These are compared byte-for-byte and hashed to prove a run is the run it
# claims to be, so git must not rewrite their line endings on checkout. Without
# this, `core.autocrlf` on a Windows clone hands back a file that differs from
# the one that was committed -- harmless to JSON.parse, fatal to "is this the
# artefact I recorded?".
runs/*.json -text

# Captured parse-server log lines are evidence too.
#
# Every line in these fixtures is real parse-server 2.8.4 output; the whole
# point of them is that they were not hand-written, so they cannot drift away
# from the log's real shape. CRLF injected on checkout would make them a file
# nobody ever measured.
test/fixtures/hook-counts/**/parse-server.* -text
